# Exclusions

## HARD EXCLUSIONS - Automatically exclude findings matching these patterns:
1. Files that are only unit tests or only used as part of running tests (unless they contain a valid secret)
2. Referencing XSS rules for non-web applications
3. Applying SQL injection rules when no database exists
4. CORS findings without any CORS implementation in the application
5. Any media files (.mp4, .mp3, .mov, .wmv, .avi, .webm, .wav, etc.)
6. Any dependency paths such as node_modules, .venv, vendor, etc.

## REPORT EXCLUSIONS - Automatically exclude these from findings report:
1. Timelines in a remediation plan. Just include the priority.
2. Recommending implementing CSP headers (unless the user asks)
3. Recommending adding HSTS headers (unless the user asks)
4. The entirety of found private keys. Only provide a short snippet of the key.
